---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { reportErrorUrl } from '../lib/report';
import { ISSUES_URL } from '../lib/site';

const countries = (await getCollection('countries')).sort((a, b) => a.data.name.localeCompare(b.data.name));
---

<Base title="Contact" description="How to reach the people behind Recreational Drones, and how to report a mistake in a country guide.">
	<div class="prose">
		<h1>Contact</h1>

		<p>
			The best way to reach us is the project's <a href={ISSUES_URL}>issue tracker on GitHub</a>. Anyone with a GitHub
			account can write there. We do not publish an email address.
		</p>

		<h2>Report a mistake in a guide</h2>
		<p>
			Rules change, and a guide can be out of date or wrong. Every guide page has a "Report a mistake" link that opens
			a new issue with the country filled in. Say what is wrong and link the official source that shows it. You can
			also pick a country here:
		</p>
		<ul class="reports">
			{countries.map((c) => <li><a href={reportErrorUrl(c.data.name, c.id)}>{c.data.name}</a></li>)}
		</ul>

		<h2>What we cannot do</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>We cannot give legal advice or say whether you may fly somewhere. Check the official source linked on each guide.</li>
			<li>We cannot help with a fine, an incident or an application. Contact the country's aviation authority, which each guide names.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.reports {
		columns: 12rem;
		padding-left: var(--space-4);
	}
	.reports a {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: var(--space-1) 0;
	}
</style>
